{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546986891,"sessionID":"ses_e2cad0faaffebn7YTy42utMRho","part":{"id":"prt_1d355e0ff0018mveBouucTg0k2","sessionID":"ses_e2cad0faaffebn7YTy42utMRho","messageID":"msg_1d355db38001U25nvgBVcGqV9i","type":"text","text":"T024 is done and both verify conditions pass.\n\n**File written** (the only file touched): `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`\n\nSix edits, all in that file:\n1. Header usage comment backfill line now ends `[--brief-only]`.\n2. `USAGE` backfill line now ends `[--brief-only]`.\n3. `parseOptions` options object gained `briefOnly: false`.\n4. `parseOptions` parses `--brief-only` as a flag after `--dry-run`.\n5. `selectMode` throws `UsageError('--brief-only needs --backfill')` when the flag is set without `--backfill`, before any mode dispatch.\n6. `backfillLog` passes `briefOnly: options.briefOnly` into `backfillRunLog`.\n\nThe guard sits at the top of `selectMode` so `node run-command-behaviour.mjs --brief-only` reaches it instead of falling through to `--runtime is required`.\n\n**Verify output**\n\n```\nrun-command-behaviour.mjs: --brief-only needs --backfill\nusage: run-command-behaviour.mjs --print-argv <runtime>\n       run-command-behaviour.mjs --list <set>\n       run-command-behaviour.mjs --runtime <runtime> (--set <set> | --row-id <id>...)\n         --out <run-log> [--arm <arm>] [--fixture <dir>] [--dry-run]\n       run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]\nexit=2\n{\"ok\":false,\"code\":\"same_path\",\"detail\":\"/Users/.../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-post-final.jsonl: the backfill writes a new log\"}\nexit=2\ncheck_exit=0\n```\n\n`node --check` exits 0. The committed log's SHA-256 was `41e878ec…b7fc1c` before and after the `same_path` run, so the refusal wrote nothing.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The working tree already held T023's changes to this same file. I left those hunks untouched and confirmed by diff that my additions are only the six above.\n- `backfillRunLog` already accepted `briefOnly` in `command-offer.mjs`, so no second file needed editing and nothing new was invented.\n- `tasks.md` was not modified, so T024's checkbox is still open.\n\n**Your next action:** nothing is blocked on you. The orchestrator can tick T024 after its own review, or leave that to the verification pass.","time":{"start":1794546983167,"end":1794546986891}}}
